The core insight is the
*identification of a compound attack surface*
from composing two individually secure retrieval modalities. Vector retrieval with tenant prefiltering is secure ( RPR = 0.0 \text{RPR}=0.0 ); graph retrieval within a single tenant's subgraph is secure. Connecting them-the pivot boundary-creates 70 70 - 194 × 194\times amplification ( AF  ( ϵ ) \text{AF}(\epsilon) ) that neither modality exhibits alone, analogous to composition vulnerabilities in other security domains. The defense implication: authorization must be placed
